ok    SSH agent           the agent on /run/user/1000/agent.sock holds 1 key (ed25519: 1)
ok    Azure CLI (az)      version 2.64.0
warn  Credential store    Puddle's file vault, key sealed with the host key by systemd, and the key no longer opens: the machine id, the host key or the Secure Boot setting changed
      note: systemd refused to open the vault key. This happens when the machine id changed (a
            cloned or restored disk image, a restore onto another computer), when systemd's host
            key (`/var/lib/systemd/credential.secret`) was lost, or when the Secure Boot setting
            changed. Restoring a Secure Boot setting brings the key back. A changed machine id
            does not: systemd deletes the host key the first time it fails to open anything, so
            restoring the old machine id no longer helps. If you cannot restore a Secure Boot
            setting, the secrets in the vault cannot be read: stop Puddle, move `secrets/vault`
            in the data folder and `puddle/vault-key.cred` in your config folder aside, start
            Puddle again and enter the secrets again.

No problems found; 1 warning to know about. (1.2 s)

